<title>JAPAN: N.Korean Defence Minister dies - official radio.</title>
<headline>N.Korean Defence Minister dies - official radio.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-02-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Korean Defence Minister Choe Kwang has died, the country's official Korea Central Radio reported on Saturday.  </p>
<p>In a broadcast monitored in Tokyo by Radiopress, which follows North Korean media, the radio said Choe died of a heart attack on Friday.</p>
<p>Choe was 78 and became defence minister in October 1995.</p>
</text>
